From: Felipe Moura <moura.fmo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] components/wpa_supplicant: Prefix AES symbols on NuttX

NuttX builds selected components into a shared flat symbol namespace.
When the software cryptodev backend enables crypto/aes.c, its
aes_encrypt() and aes_decrypt() symbols collide with the wpa_supplicant
mbedTLS crypto wrapper.

Prefix the wpa_supplicant AES block helpers when building for NuttX so
the ESP Wi-Fi stack can coexist with NuttX's software crypto
implementation.

Signed-off-by: Felipe Moura <moura.fmo@gmail.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/espressif/esp-hal-3rdparty/commit/1e9759ca6fbdd22fcadd7108aaab6f4daca1345f
Upstream-PR: https://github.com/espressif/esp-hal-3rdparty/pull/13
Base: b90b1837cb5ad24747deb4c895246037cc206ce5

Exact upstream source diff; backported without changing the dependency pin.

diff --git a/components/wpa_supplicant/src/crypto/aes.h b/components/wpa_supplicant/src/crypto/aes.h
--- a/components/wpa_supplicant/src/crypto/aes.h
+++ b/components/wpa_supplicant/src/crypto/aes.h
@@ -11,6 +11,12 @@
 
 #ifdef __NuttX__
 #include "utils/common.h"
+#define aes_encrypt_init esp_wpa_aes_encrypt_init
+#define aes_encrypt esp_wpa_aes_encrypt
+#define aes_encrypt_deinit esp_wpa_aes_encrypt_deinit
+#define aes_decrypt_init esp_wpa_aes_decrypt_init
+#define aes_decrypt esp_wpa_aes_decrypt
+#define aes_decrypt_deinit esp_wpa_aes_decrypt_deinit
 #endif
 
 #define AES_BLOCK_SIZE 16
diff --git a/components/wpa_supplicant/src/crypto/crypto.h b/components/wpa_supplicant/src/crypto/crypto.h
--- a/components/wpa_supplicant/src/crypto/crypto.h
+++ b/components/wpa_supplicant/src/crypto/crypto.h
@@ -22,6 +22,15 @@
 #define CRYPTO_H
 #include "utils/common.h"
 
+#ifdef __NuttX__
+#define aes_encrypt_init esp_wpa_aes_encrypt_init
+#define aes_encrypt esp_wpa_aes_encrypt
+#define aes_encrypt_deinit esp_wpa_aes_encrypt_deinit
+#define aes_decrypt_init esp_wpa_aes_decrypt_init
+#define aes_decrypt esp_wpa_aes_decrypt
+#define aes_decrypt_deinit esp_wpa_aes_decrypt_deinit
+#endif
+
 /**
  * md4_vector - MD4 hash for data vector
  * @num_elem: Number of elements in the data vector

